-- title:
--   Cone membership is positivity of the cone gap
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a real inner product space, $v \in E$ a unit vector ($\|v\| = 1$) and $\vartheta$ an apex angle with $0 < \vartheta \le \pi/2$. Write $\mathcal{C}(v,\vartheta)$ for the open circular cone with axis $v$ and half-angle $\vartheta$ (`cone v ϑ`), and for $p \in E$ let
--   $$g_{v,\vartheta}(p) \;=\; \langle v, p\rangle \sin\vartheta \;-\; \bigl\|\,p - \langle v,p\rangle\, v\,\bigr\| \cos\vartheta$$
--   be the *cone gap* of $p$ (`coneGap v ϑ p`), formed from the component $a = \langle v,p\rangle$ of $p$ along the axis and the component $b = \|p - a v\|$ across it as $a \sin\vartheta - b\cos\vartheta$. The claim is the equivalence
--   $$p \in \mathcal{C}(v,\vartheta) \iff g_{v,\vartheta}(p) > 0 .$$
--
--   The cone gap is a signed distance to the boundary of the cone, and this equivalence identifies the cone as exactly the region where that signed distance is positive. It is the qualitative half of the cone-gap calculus: the quantitative half turns a positive gap into an inscribed ball of that radius, and together they replace angular arguments about cones by an inequality between two linear-in-$p$ quantities.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/ConeGap.lean#L44-L74

